==English==

===Etymology===
From Latin '''plectrum''', from [[Ancient Greek]] '''[[πλήκτρον]]''' {{italbrac|pléktron}} “anything to strike with,  an instrument for striking the lyre, a spear point”, from '''[[πλήσσειν]]''' {{italbrac|pléssein}} “to strike, to smite, to sting”.

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
'''plectrum''' or '''plectron''' (''plural'' '''[[plectra]]''')

# a small piece of plastic, metal, ivory, etc for [[pluck]]ing the [[string]]s of a [[guitar]], [[lyre]], [[mandolin]], etc
# {{context|Anatomy|Zoology}} an [[anatomical]] part resembling a [[plectrum]] in shape

====Synonyms====
*[[pick]] (US)

